<DocsLayout title="Pydantic AI guide | Agent-Gantry" description="Integrate Agent-Gantry with Pydantic AI 2.x through a native Capability, toolset or Gantry-backed ToolSearch.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Framework guide</p>
  <h1>Pydantic AI</h1>
  <p class="lead">Agent-Gantry plugs into Pydantic AI 2.x through its own extension points: a <code>Capability</code>, an <code>AbstractToolset</code> that re-selects tools on every model step, and a <code>ToolSearch</code> strategy backed by Gantry's semantic router. Tool failures, approvals, <code>deps</code> and tracing all use Pydantic AI's native mechanisms.</p>
  <p><a class="pill" href="/Agent-Gantry/docs/frameworks/pydantic-ai/advanced/">Advanced Pydantic AI usage →</a></p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`uv add "agent-gantry[pydantic-ai]"   # pins pydantic-ai-slim>=2.0.0`} />

  <h2>Basic page: one capability</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Register tools with <code>@gantry.register</code> and <code>await gantry.sync()</code>.</li>
    <li>Add <code>adapter.capability()</code> to your agent's <code>capabilities</code>.</li>
    <li>Run the agent normally. Each model step sees only the top-k relevant tools, re-selected from the newest prompt or tool result.</li>
  </ol>
  <CodeBlock lang="python" title="Per-turn tool selection" code={`import asyncio

from pydantic_ai import Agent
from agent_gantry import AgentGantry
from agent_gantry.pydantic_ai import PydanticAIAdapter

gantry = AgentGantry()

@gantry.register(examples=["where is my order", "has order 4471 shipped"])
def get_order_status(order_id: str) -> str:
    """Return the current shipping status for an order."""
    return "in_transit"

@gantry.register(examples=["refund order 4471"], requires_confirmation=True)
def refund_order(order_id: str) -> str:
    """Refund an order in full."""
    return "refunded"

async def main():
    await gantry.sync()
    adapter = PydanticAIAdapter(gantry)
    agent = Agent("openai:gpt-5.5", capabilities=[adapter.capability(limit=5)])
    result = await agent.run("Has order 4471 shipped?")
    print(result.output)

asyncio.run(main())`} />

  <h2>Choosing a mode</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Per-turn</strong> (<code>adapter.capability()</code> or <code>Agent(toolsets=[adapter.toolset()])</code>): Gantry pushes a fresh top-k each step. After a tool returns, the next selection reads its result, so a chained task ("look up the customer, then email them") surfaces the next tool mid-run.</li>
    <li><strong>Search</strong> (<code>adapter.capability(mode="search")</code>): the whole catalogue is deferred behind Pydantic AI's <code>search_tools</code>, and Gantry ranks what it returns. The tool list stays stable between turns, so provider prompt caching survives. Prefer it for large catalogues.</li>
    <li><strong>Static</strong> (<code>Agent(tools=await adapter.select(query))</code>): one selection up front, for fixed tasks.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What the model sees when a tool fails</h2>
  <p>Pydantic AI ends a run on an ordinary exception from a tool, so Gantry maps its outcomes to Pydantic AI's own exceptions instead:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Bad arguments</strong> become <code>ModelRetry</code>, so the model corrects its call within the tool's retry budget.</li>
    <li><strong>Terminal failures</strong> (handler errors, timeouts, open circuit breakers, policy denials) become <code>ToolFailed</code>. The model sees the error and adapts.</li>
    <li><strong>Confirmation-gated calls</strong> become <code>ApprovalRequired</code>. See the advanced page for the approval flow.</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="callout"><strong>Opt out:</strong> pass <code>error_mode="raise"</code> to the adapter or any builder to let <code>ToolExecutionError</code> propagate instead, matching the other framework adapters.</div>

  <h2>Reading <code>deps</code> from a Gantry tool</h2>
  <p>Gantry tools keep their own schema; the run's <code>RunContext</code> is available ambiently while the call executes.</p>
  <CodeBlock lang="python" code={`from agent_gantry.pydantic_ai import current_run_context

@gantry.register
async def get_balance(account: str) -> str:
    """Fetch an account balance for the signed-in user."""
    ctx = current_run_context()   # pydantic_ai.RunContext, or None outside a run
    return await ctx.deps.bank.balance(account)`} />
